   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Disclaimer: this is the first time I try this test.<div><br></div><div>Looking at the example in MKmisc::<span style=\"font-size:12.8px;text-align:right\">HLgof.test(), it that the test statistic is exactly the one described in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hosmer%E2%80%93Lemeshow_test\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hosmer%25E2%2580%2593Lemeshow_test&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496894725000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3EN5ryHJaQDy4NqPWylsEt\">Wiki</a>.</span></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">You say that SPSS in underpowered? And that it is due to some normalization which is not performed in R.</span></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Could you explain your claim in terms of the formula in the Wiki?</span></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"></div>"
    ],
